## STOP-and-report: a live blocker the SIT spec found

`sit/integration/longevity-prescribe-surface.integration.test.ts` ran against live Medplum and is **RED on the supplement route**, for a real product defect outside this route's scope guard:

`assignSupplementPlan` (`src/lib/clinical/supplements/supplement-protocol-crud.ts:70-80`) builds `CarePlan.activity[0]` with **both** `reference` and `detail`, violating FHIR invariant **cpl-3**. MockClient enforces no invariants so every unit suite is green; the live server 400s the CarePlan entry while the ServiceRequest in the same transaction still commits (non-atomic), leaving an orphan ServiceRequest and no plan. It had no UI consumer until this brief, so mounting the surface is what exposed it.

I did **not** fix it — it's outside §1's affected surface — and I did not weaken the assertion to green. The spec's header documents the diagnosis; the lifestyle and drug routes were verified landing live in the same session and have their own green tests. This needs a one-line follow-up brief. (It's the second instance of the cpl-3 pattern; `materializeCarePlan` has the same bug per the existing note, which I've extended.)

Two smaller flags: the brief's §3.4 says "Lucide icons", but the repo has no `lucide-react` and the house pattern uses `@tabler/icons-react` — I followed the house pattern. And the section renders only for an enrolled patient (`useLongevityRowData`), matching D-S7CORE5-03 and the other two L capture surfaces; say the word if the prescribe surface should instead be unconditional.

